    {
      "id": "p3",
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Problem 3",
      "sourcePages": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You have to tile a room that is two units wide and $N$ units long. You have with you two types of tiles: a rectangle that is one unit wide and two units long, and an L-shaped tile covering three square units. Here are pictures of the two types of tiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2006-p3-tiles.png",
          "alt": "The two tile types: a 1 × 2 rectangle and an L-shaped tile covering three squares.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You are allowed to rotate the tiles when you lay them. You have an infinite supply of both types of tiles. Your objective is to calculate the number of different ways of tiling the room using these tiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "For instance, a 2 × 3 room can be tiled in 5 different ways, as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2006-p3-ways.png",
          "alt": "The five ways to tile a 2 × 3 room.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Notice that a tiling can use both types of tiles. Consider, for instance, the following tiling of a 2 × 4 room."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2006-p3-example.png",
          "alt": "A tiling of a 2 × 4 room using both an L-shaped tile and rectangular tiles.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Calculate the number of different ways of tiling rooms of the following sizes."
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "p3a",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "2 × 8",
          "answerType": "integer",
          "officialAnswer": "258",
